--
--   Test Description
--   This test checks the receive status and network control registers.  
--   Furthermore, the receive buffer locations starting on a 32-byte 
--   boundary and the frame discard functionality are also tested.
--
--   Functional Coverage
--   � Ensures the GEM receive functionality works properly with the DMA
--   � Ensures the receive status and network control register are working 
--     properly.
--   � Tests buffer locations starting on a 32-byte boundary.
--   � Ensures the frame discard functionality works properly.
--
--   Detailed Test Description
--
--    1. Initialise the GEM for 10 or 100-mode operation.
--    2. Check the receive status and control registers.
--    3. Write an address to specific address register one.
--    4. Receive a specifically address matched frame with receive. (All 
--       buffer locations start on the 32-byte boundary)
--    5. Clear the receive status register.
--    6. Receive a runt preamble for code coverage
--    7. Receive a broadcast frame. (Frame should be stored to memory)
--    8. Receive a broadcast frame with an incorrect destination address.
--       This frame should be discarded.
--    9. Receive a broadcast frame. This frame should be written to memory.
--   10. Read another receive buffer descriptor with the used bit set. This
--       should cause a rx used bit read interrupt to be set. Also, the
--       receive status register should indicate that a receive buffer was
--       not available.
--   11. Receive a frame.  The buffer descriptor read has the ownership bit set.
--       Therefore, this frame should be discarded. The rx used bit read
--       interrupt should be set.
--   12. Receive a frame. The buffer descriptor read does not have the
--       ownership bit set. Therefore, this frame should be written to memory.
--   13. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure the above
--       operations were handled properly.
--   14. Whilst receiving a frame, disable receive. The frame should be 
--       discarded
--   15. Enable the GEM to receive frames.
--   16. Receive a frame. The frame should be written to memory.
--   17. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure the above
--       operations were handled properly.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

pinsc(50) loopback 0 half_duplex 1  extint 0 --  check reset state


-- *****************************************************************************
--    1. Initialise the GEM for 10 or 100-mode operation.
--    2. Check the receive status and control registers.
--    3. Write an address to specific address register one.
-- *****************************************************************************
apbrd(100) 00 00000000  -- check reset value of network control register
apbrd      18 00000000  -- check reset value of receive queue pointer
apbwr      18 01234000  -- write receive queue pointer
apbwr      4ec 0000000f -- set the RX descriptor trigger rate to very slow, otherwise it changes the behaviour of this test.
apbwr      00 00000004  -- enable receive
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      28 ffffffff  -- enable all interrupts
apbrd      24 00000000  -- check interrupt status
apbwr      98 12345678  -- specific address register 3 bottom
apbwr      9C 00001111  -- specific address register 3 top
apbrd      04 00080000  -- check reset value of network config register
apbrd      08 00000006  -- check reset value of network status register


-- *****************************************************************************
--    4. Receive a specifically address matched frame with receive. (All 
--       buffer locations start on the 32-byte boundary)
-- *****************************************************************************

